        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel, Lebanon united in liberating Lebanon from Hezbollah, Israeli ambassador to US says Middle East Issued on: 14/04/2026 - 20:52 ⁠The ​Lebanese government made ​it clear during U.S.-brokered talks ​with ‌Israel ⁠that ‌they no longer want to ⁠be \"occupied\" by Hezbollah and ​that ‌there were conversations about long-term ‌vision for ​clearly delineated border, Israel's ambassador to the ​United States ​Yechiel ​Leiter told reporters on ​Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem. Italian PM says suspends renewal of defence agreement with Israel 14/04/2026 Middle East Donald Trump 'hasn't read the psychology of Iranians well at all', military expert says 13/04/2026 Middle East Lebanon will need '1 billion dollars just to keep humanitarian situation afloat', minister says 13/04/2026 Middle East Netanyahu in southern Lebanon: A first since the start of the war 13/04/2026 Middle East Lebanese govt politically present, operationally absent': PM accuses Israel of violating int'l law' 12/04/2026 Middle East Trump says US will begin 'blockading' the Strait of Hormuz 12/04/2026 Middle East Iran believes they hold the cards amid 'dysfunction & chaos in US national security decision-making' 12/04/2026 Middle East Trump orders blockade of Hormuz Strait 12/04/2026 Middle East US, Iran fail to agree on peace deal 12/04/2026 Middle East"
